      "content": "That's the full final report from the coder agent — it lines up exactly with what I already confirmed directly (merge `e5121168...` landed, CI 12/12 green, sibling repos untouched). Two things worth flagging beyond my earlier summary:\n\n**A real, non-trivial bug found and fixed**: `GlobalHeaderV2` itself has no resize listener — closing the mobile menu via viewport resize left `body.style.overflow` permanently stuck at `hidden` (a real scroll-lock bug, verified with a throwaway Playwright script showing the before/after state). Fixed locally in Code's integration via a `key`-driven remount. Since this is a bug in the *shared library itself*, not just Code's usage of it, it likely also affects Claw and Gate's already-merged integrations — worth deciding whether to backport the fix upstream into `aisyndicate-ui` rather than leaving it as a per-site workaround.\n\n**Glyph**: `SquareTerminal`, not `Terminal`/`SquareCode` as I'd suggested as options — reasoned as \"a bounded terminal shape signals contained, operator-visible session\" better than generic code brackets. Also flagged: JetBrains Mono was kept (not dropped) because Code has genuine, extensive monospace content (CLI examples, terminal displays) — correctly following the \"keep only if actually needed\" rule from the spec.\n\nThe agent also wrote 4 memory entries to its own `.claude/agent-memory/coder/` — separate from your account-level Honcho memory, scoped to that agent role.",
