      "createdAt": "2026-08-21T17:59:49.200000Z"
    },
    {
      "content": "Pushed clean (no pre-push hook here, per this repo's CLAUDE.md — no separate lint/test job). Opening the MR.",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-23T12:09:38.016000Z"
    },
    {
      "content": "Discovery running on both Code and Gate — fresh state on their headers, fonts, homepage copy, accent overrides, and a check for whether either has the same latent dependency-CVE gate issue that blocked Claw earlier. I'll draft the plan once it lands.",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-23T16:50:31.832000Z"
    },
    {
      "content": "```\n05fd6d1 build(deps): bump the production-dependencies group with 2 updates (#64)\n98e5727 security: restrict CI workflow token permissions\n9cacdfc docs: record completed four-property corpus\n18d5a3c release: v1.14.0\n944a2f2 feat: add demo mode, answer-engine claim diff, registry seeds, and checklist consolidation\n```",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-03T08:59:54.826000Z"
    }
  ],
  "conclusions": [
    {
      "id": "GF_h2lSkK-pI4E_MNE2ef",
      "content": "Values minimal, root-cause-focused code changes above all — smallest diff that solves the problem, no temporary fixes or scope creep, consistent with their global CLAUDE.md principles (Simplicity First, Minimal Impact, No Laziness).",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-25T14:50:18.377662Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "9CN-u4z8o35GMfGXTmsCI",
      "content": "mike is reviewing the relevant existing research and evidence, including at least first dogfood campaign, six-remediation candidate, independent review of that candidate, context correctness fixes, C2 observation-reference experiment, investigation-targeting experiment, E3 evidence-to-decision experiment, E4 evidence-delivery ordering experiment, comparative open-source harness review, and any available research concerning closed-source harness maturity trajectories.",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-06T05:44:49.461366Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "Fj3nKoOlBnDZYwoUnQyMA",
      "content": "mike is inspecting current open-source implementations including OpenCode, Charmbracelet Crush, Aider, and Cline.",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-03T20:23:05.771765Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "4jgK2i8mOa7ySim3yBFP8",
      "content": "In the 2026-10-04 Nexus Phase 3 session mike operates as a read-only independent verification layer rather than an implementer: he is explicitly the independent investigation/review agent running in parallel with Cursor's Phase 3 execution, barred from modifying Cursor's worktree or branch, barred from merging/rebase/cherry-picking Cursor's work, barred from modifying, coordinating, redirecting or interfering with Cursor's active work, and barred from pushing, publishing, tagging or deploying. The separation exists so his evidence about the four defects remains independent of the implementing agent's changes.",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-04T10:54:57.146718Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "xj5GgyKuwV0t4VX52Qa_k",
      "content": "mike is using prior open-source harness research as mechanism evidence.",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-06T05:44:49.461366Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "4b_1BtA29ICz8o5zADyAD",
      "content": "mike updated the software (likely the Claude CLI or n8n integration tool) multiple times, progressing from version 2.1.215 on July 24, 2026, to version 2.1.220 by July 26, 2026.",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-26T19:38:34.297087Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "JxUS4t9ljr4cVwO-3eczO",
      "content": "mikeholownych/hermes-agent has upstream NousResearch references untouched",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-31T20:06:26.187350Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "8o7G9tG-Ly_Lraw1AYUfn",
      "content": "mike is using closed-source changelog/release-history research only for what it can actually establish.",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-06T05:44:49.461366Z"
    }
  ]
}

